A busy morning brings hundreds of reports about the same thing. We keep one ticket per issue
and merge every duplicate into it, so engineering sees one thread with a count.

<Callout kind="warn">
The review of #4471 contradicts the subject-only rule recorded below.
Use the cause-based procedure in <a href="/kb/incidents/4471-review">the signed review</a>
while the desk considers <a href="/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause">decision 0002</a>.
</Callout>

## Historical rule from decision 0001

A report is a duplicate when its **subject line matches** the subject of an open ticket
([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)):

1. lowercase the subject and strip punctuation;
2. look for an open ticket with the same subject;
3. found one: merge the report into it. None: open a new ticket.

This was the old rule. The cause comparison below demonstrates why the subject is insufficient.

## Try it

<DedupeExplorer />

## When you are unsure

Keep reports separate until the cause is understood. Preserve report IDs and evidence;
ask for the missing tenant or reproduction information before merging.
